{"request_sha256": "7368c69bab54814371f910adeefecf7c2cc686b85371fc33f9695ed692aac2d6", "prompt_sha256": "847dd718e56258447ec5fcc89fdaadc9701165d02eab0b51001e616ebc1a0329", "dispatched_prompt_sha256": "a1cbedbd0e473a81ec8ba7fddb865c007c99e9e942abedd93954d2af058abb5c", "schema_sha256": "30f41622e6c7560e23f9cf8ab8aee356761b3ddea7cb1a9d1835cabc34f30ac0", "model": "opus", "model_identity_basis": "claude CLI result event modelUsage key: claude-opus-5", "effort": "medium", "status": "ok", "forbidden_tools": [], "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 6462}, "answer": {"passes": ["fail", "fail", "fail", "unknown", "fail", "fail", "fail", "fail", "pass", "pass"], "defects": ["Crown reads as a flat starburst of very short, thin, straight rays rather than a palm rosette of long arching pinnate fronds; no frond droops below the crown base in either seed (render-0, render-1 vs reference-0).", "Frond length is a small fraction of trunk length (crown spread roughly 1/5 of tree height, fronds shorter than ~1.5 trunk diameters of visible extension), where reference-0 shows fronds a substantial fraction of trunk length and a crown several times the trunk width.", "Leaflets render as sparse dotted/speckled fragments along a bare rachis rather than dense narrow stiff leaflets forming a continuous plumose V-sectioned blade (render-0, render-1, render-2 vs reference-0, reference-1, reference-2).", "Trunk is visibly wavy: a sinuous S in the upper half plus a pronounced kink/elbow at roughly mid-height, clearest in render-2, present in both whole-view seeds.", "Trunk diameter is far from constant: it is widest at ground level and narrows markedly toward the crown, a continuous taper rather than the columnar near-constant stem of reference-0/1/2.", "Trunk surface is smooth and untextured: no retained leaf-base stubs, no spiral diamond/rhomboid lattice, no fibrous matting anywhere along its length (render-2 vs reference-1, reference-2).", "No pendent fruiting bunches are present below the crown in any render, where reference-0 shows two to three heavy orange bunches on thick downward-bending stalks.", "The P-BASE render (render-3) is a near-black, featureless slab filling the frame with no resolvable surface detail; it is also flagged visibility=hidden in the joint inputs, so the leaf-base close cell cannot be assessed."], "observations": ["Both whole views (seed 1 and seed 42) show the same structural character; the seed difference changes trunk curvature amplitude slightly but not the crown or trunk verdicts.", "The crown rays radiate near-symmetrically in a disc around the apex, including rays pointing upward and horizontally, with the lowest rays roughly horizontal or only slightly below horizontal; none recurve downward past the crown base.", "Foliage colour in the renders is a dark green with black speckling; reference foliage spans deep green (reference-0) to grey-glaucous (reference-1, reference-2). Colour is not treated as a defining mismatch here.", "The trunk carries nothing: no epiphytic ferns, vines, seedlings, or attached foliage at any height in either seed. This matches the owner requirement and is also consistent with reference-0; the ferns in reference-1/reference-2 are inventory-marked scene variation, not species character.", "A single unbranched stem carries the crown in all renders; no branching appears anywhere.", "Against the fn9 spruce anchor (anchor-0), the render's foliage reads as scattered dot/dash primitives with visible aliasing rather than the anchor's coherent needle mass; this is a finish-quality observation only and carries no morphology weight.", "The inventory's own note that trunk organs are not yet expressed by the generator is recorded, but the assessment here is of what is drawn: the drawn trunk is smooth and bare of leaf bases.", "Relative to the described prior state the fronds may be longer, but absolute frond length and leaflet size remain far below reference character; improvement is not scored."], "findings": [{"observation": "Crown is a flat radial starburst of short, thin, sparsely-leafleted rays; no long arching fronds and no drooping lower fronds in either seed.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Consistent with frond length and leaflet size dials still being set low, as the owner notes; the mechanism is not established by the images."}, {"observation": "Trunk is sinuous with a distinct mid-height elbow and tapers continuously from a wide base to a narrow apex.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Possibly the taper dial sitting at 1.0, outside the authored 0.05-0.6 range noted by the host; not established from the images alone."}, {"observation": "Trunk surface is entirely smooth: no leaf-base stubs, no spiral diamond lattice, no fibrous matting.", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Matches the stated fn-110 trunk-organ work not having landed; reported as observed absence, not inferred from the plan."}, {"observation": "No pendent fruit bunches anywhere below the crown.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": "Consistent with the date cluster (fn-111) not being landed; descoped by the owner for this pass but still an unmatched core reference trait."}, {"observation": "Trunk carries no foliage, epiphytes, or growths at any height, in both seeds.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Single unbranched stem carrying one apical crown.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0"], "impact": "supported", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "P-BASE render is a near-black featureless slab with no resolvable detail and is flagged visibility=hidden.", "evidence_ids": ["render-3", "reference-2"], "impact": "required_unknown", "uncertain": true, "causal_hypothesis": "Could be extreme close framing plus underexposure/clipping of the shadow side, or the flagged hidden visibility; not determinable from the image."}, {"observation": "Foliage renders as speckled dot primitives with aliasing, below the coherent foliage mass of the fn9 spruce anchor.", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "anchor-0"], "impact": "optional", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}, {"observation": "Trunk lean and curvature are inventory-marked variation, but the render's waviness exceeds the observed reference range: reference-0 is a smooth single lean/curve, reference-1 and reference-2 are straight and vertical; no reference shows a localized elbow.", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "impact": "blocker", "uncertain": false, "causal_hypothesis": null}], "coverage": [{"trait_id": "crown-pinnate-arching-fronds", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Reference crowns are rounded hemispherical/shuttlecock masses of many long fronds, older ones recurving well below the crown base. The render shows roughly 20-30 short straight rays in a near-planar disc, with the lowest rays at or just below horizontal and none arching downward. Defining mismatch of crown character, not an optional refinement."}, {"trait_id": "leaflet-arrangement-stiff-narrow", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "References show dense narrow stiff leaflets inserted in groups at differing angles, giving a continuous plumose blade with a bristly margin. The render's rachises carry sparse detached dot/dash fragments with large gaps; no continuous blade and no plumose V-section reads at either whole or trunk framing. Defining mismatch."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-leaf-base-diamond-pattern", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-0", "reference-1", "reference-2", "reference-0"], "explanation": "The drawn trunk is a smooth untextured surface over its whole visible length at close framing; no stubs, no spiral, no diamond lattice, and not even the finer knobbly distance texture of reference-0. Assessed as drawn rather than dismissed as pending work: core trait unmatched."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-fibrous-matting", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "No fibre, husk, or shaggy interstitial material is present on the rendered trunk; the surface is uniformly smooth. Core trait unmatched."}, {"trait_id": "solitary-columnar-stem", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "The solitary unbranched half of this trait is supported: one stem, no branching anywhere. The columnar, roughly-constant-diameter half is not: the render narrows continuously from a wide ground-level base to a narrow apex and is sinuous with a mid-height elbow. Because the inventory states this trait as a single unbranched column of roughly constant diameter, the cell fails on the diameter/column character."}, {"trait_id": "fruit-clusters-pendent", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Reference-0 shows two to three heavy orange-red pendent bunches on thick downward-bending stalks among the frond bases. Neither whole-view render shows any inflorescence or fruit structure. The owner descoped the date cluster (fn-111) for this pass; that scopes the work, not the trait, so this is recorded as an unmatched core trait rather than silently dropped."}, {"trait_id": "dead-frond-skirt", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Secondary trait. No brown collar of dead fronds below the living crown in either seed; the crown-to-trunk junction is bare. Not a blocker at this priority."}, {"trait_id": "petiole-base-orange-sheath", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Secondary trait. The crown apex in the closest available framing (render-2) resolves only dark rachis stubs against the trunk; no petiole base colour or sheath material is separable at this resolution."}, {"trait_id": "crown-shaft-absent", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Secondary trait. No smooth green crownshaft is present in the render; the frond bases sit directly on the trunk, matching the reference. Supported, though trivially so given the trunk carries no surface detail at all."}, {"trait_id": "basal-leaflet-spines", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Secondary and inventory-marked uncertain. The proximal ends of the rendered rays are bare, but leaflet primitives are too coarse and sparse throughout to distinguish an authored spine zone from general leaflet sparsity."}, {"trait_id": "basal-flare", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-3", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Secondary and inventory-marked uncertain. The whole views show the trunk widening near the ground, but that widening is inseparable from the render's overall continuous taper, and the dedicated base view (render-3) is unreadable, so a genuine basal flare cannot be confirmed."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-colour-and-weathering", "status": "unknown", "evidence_ids": ["render-2", "render-3", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "The rendered trunk reads dark brown to near-black with the lit edge warm brown, but render-3 is clipped to black and the shaded face dominates elsewhere, so colour range and weathering cannot be fairly compared against the references."}, {"trait_id": "frond-colour-range", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Variation trait. The render's dark to mid green sits inside the observed reference span from deep green to grey-glaucous. Acceptable variation, not defining character."}, {"trait_id": "trunk-lean-and-curve", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0", "reference-1", "reference-2"], "explanation": "Variation trait, but the render falls outside the observed range rather than within it. References span a smooth single lean/S-curve (reference-0) to straight vertical (reference-1, reference-2); the render adds a localized mid-height elbow and upper-trunk waviness seen in no reference, and the owner explicitly rules out waviness."}, {"trait_id": "epiphytes-on-trunk", "status": "pass", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "render-2", "reference-0"], "explanation": "Variation trait, present in reference-1/reference-2 and absent in reference-0. The render's bare trunk sits within that range and satisfies the owner's requirement that nothing grow on the trunk."}, {"trait_id": "crown-silhouette-proportions", "status": "fail", "evidence_ids": ["render-0", "render-1", "reference-0", "reference-1"], "explanation": "Inventory lists this as variation with unmeasurable exact ratios, but the render is outside even a generous band: crown spread is roughly a fifth of tree height and the crown mass is a small tuft on a very long stem, where reference-0 shows a crown several times the trunk width with fronds a substantial fraction of trunk length. This is the same deficit the owner named first."}]}, "raw_events": "{"type":"system","subtype":"init","cwd":"/home/daniel/Projects/telperion/.worktrees/fn-80-the-gap-loops-first-live-run","session_id":"3eb34232-02e1-4eec-9d53-84aafc1e327b","tools":["StructuredOutput"],"mcp_s